      "writtenOn": "2018-09-13T14:01:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Lots of variables and bit fiddling here, not exactly readable (e.g. num_siblings is used both as a count and a mask). The way we made this readable in cryptohome was to introduce Label class that simplifies working with labels. See https://chromium.git.corp.google.com/chromiumos/platform2/+/95812fdebefc538a79bd84913aa15af6b2344775/cryptohome/sign_in_hash_tree.cc#73 for the corresponding code (which is much clearer to read IMHO).\n\nI\u0027m not sure there\u0027s a good way to share this code, but it would probably be better than re-implementing all this. platform/ec depending on cryptohome would be backwards. Maybe it makes sense to break the fuzzer out into a separate package that can pull both cryptohome bits and platform/ec?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 29,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 49,
        "endChar": 69
      },
